// The duel's moves: each one's rules (`engine::combat::Move`: its wind-up, its hitting ticks and
// its recovery, its reach and what it does) and its drawing (`pose::Beat`s keyed on the same
// ticks, so a fist is out exactly while it can hit).
//
// The wanderer's are quick and cheap (a jab, a cross, a hook to the body): a fight is won by
// answering, not trading. The brawler's are slow, heavy and readable, and each tells its timing in
// its silhouette: a one-two; a haymaker raised high and held there (the genre's delayed blow: a
// dodge on the lift is too early); a lunge from far off; a sweep low and wide.

use engine::clip::{HOLD, SMOOTH, SNAP}
use engine::combat::Move
use pose::Beat
use poses::{
    COIL, CROSS, CROSS_LOAD, GUARD, HAY_COCKED, HAY_DOWN, HAY_LIFT, HOOK, HOOK_LOAD, JAB, JAB_LOAD,
    LUNGE, LUNGE_LOAD, OVERHEAD, SWEEP, SWEEP_WIND, UPPERCUT,
}

